            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "It seems that the behavior can be minimally reproduced like this. Create three text files, such as `1.txt 2.txt 3.txt`, containing only a single pair of parentheses `()`. The first file can actually contain anything (including nothing). Then open the three files at once (`nvim 1.txt 2.txt 3.txt`) with mini.diff enabled.\r\n\r\nMy suspicion is that if a file starts with a matched delimiter, the built-in MatchIt plugin somehow breaks due to all the buffers being activated by mini.diff.",
