            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue, Adam!\r\n\r\nThis seems to happen due to the fact that `vim.fn.bufload()` triggers `BufWinEnter` event which has callbacks from 'matchparen'. As those buffers are shown in the same special \"autocommand\" window, they might conflict. Which is extra weird because adding match with id 3 is done only [if there is no `vim.fn.matchaddpos()`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/889f81c65fa4318ab0fba391904dc43e5633b13e/runtime/plugin/matchparen.vim#L198-L199).\r\n\r\nNevertheless, loading buffers should indeed be done more carefully. Would you mind applying the following patch to 'mini.diff' and see if this solves the issue:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/diff.lua b/lua/mini/diff.lua\r\nindex 42eaffb..a608844 100644\r\n--- a/lua/mini/diff.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/diff.lua\r\n@@ -435,7 +435,7 @@ MiniDiff.enable = function(buf_id)\r\n   if H.is_buf_enabled(buf_id) or H.is_disabled(buf_id) then return end\r\n\r\n   -- Ensure buffer is loaded (to have up to date lines returned)\r\n-  if not vim.api.nvim_buf_is_loaded(buf_id) then vim.fn.bufload(buf_id) end\r\n+  H.buf_ensure_loaded(buf_id)\r\n\r\n   -- Register enabled buffer with cached data for performance\r\n   H.update_buf_cache(buf_id)\r\n@@ -1697,6 +1697,14 @@ H.error = function(msg) error(string.format('(mini.diff) %s', msg), 0) end\r\n\r\n H.notify = function(msg, level_name) vim.notify('(mini.diff) ' .. msg, vim.log.levels[level_name]) end\r\n\r\n+H.buf_ensure_loaded = function(buf_id)\r\n+  if type(buf_id) ~= 'number' or vim.api.nvim_buf_is_loaded(buf_id) then return end\r\n+  local cache_eventignore = vim.o.eventignore\r\n+  vim.o.eventignore = 'BufEnter,BufWinEnter'\r\n+  pcall(vim.fn.bufload, buf_id)\r\n+  vim.o.eventignore = cache_eventignore\r\n+end\r\n+\r\n H.map = function(mode, lhs, rhs, opts)\r\n   if lhs == '' then return end\r\n   opts = vim.tbl_deep_extend('force', { silent = true }, opts or {})\r\n```",
